[2026-09-20 10:42:01 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 011] --------------------------------------------------------------------------------
[2026-09-20 10:42:01 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 011]   TEP / Planet-9 -- step 03: field-wall vs point-mass discriminators
[2026-09-20 10:42:01 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 011]   The two candidate explanations of the extreme-TNO clustering make
[2026-09-20 10:42:01 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 011]   different structural predictions for the same catalog:
[2026-09-20 10:42:01 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 011]   Point mass (Planet 9): a moving perturber shepherds orbits.  It
[2026-09-20 10:42:01 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 011]   couples to all orbital elements through Newtonian dynamics;
[2026-09-20 10:42:01 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 011]   confinement should strengthen with semimajor axis; surviving
[2026-09-20 10:42:01 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 011]   objects are expected to occupy mean-motion resonances with the
[2026-09-20 10:42:01 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 011]   perturber (resonant substructure in a); non-aligned objects are
[2026-09-20 10:42:01 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 011]   transitional, scattered smoothly.
[2026-09-20 10:42:01 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 011]   Temporal field boundary (TEP): a spatially fixed lapse gradient.
[2026-09-20 10:42:01 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 011]   Its gradient has one direction in inertial space, so the anomaly
[2026-09-20 10:42:01 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 011]   concentrates in the clock-like elements (perihelion longitudes,
[2026-09-20 10:42:01 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 011]   nodal phases) rather than the geometric elements; selection is by
[2026-09-20 10:42:01 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 011]   *crossing*, so membership should have a sharp edge in the variable
[2026-09-20 10:42:01 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 011]   that controls crossing (perihelion/aphelion geometry), not a smooth
[2026-09-20 10:42:01 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 011]   gradient in a; semimajor axes should be smooth (no resonances);
[2026-09-20 10:42:01 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 011]   every population that crosses the boundary shares the axis.
[2026-09-20 10:42:01 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 011]   Tests implemented on the detached sample (a>150 AU, q>30 AU,
[2026-09-20 10:42:01 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 011]   condition_code<=3):
[2026-09-20 10:42:01 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 011]   D1  Element selectivity: conditioned-MC significance separately for
[2026-09-20 10:42:01 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 011]   node om, argument w, longitude varpi, perihelion vector phat and
[2026-09-20 10:42:01 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 011]   folded pole nhat.
[2026-09-20 10:42:01 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 011]   D2  Clustered-mixture structure: uniform + von Mises fit to varpi;
[2026-09-20 10:42:01 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 011]   clustered fraction, center, concentration kappa.
[2026-09-20 10:42:01 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 011]   D3  Membership predictor: is alignment with the mean axis controlled
[2026-09-20 10:42:01 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 011]   by a (shepherding expectation) or by the crossing variables
[2026-09-20 10:42:01 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 011]   q, aphelion ad?  Spearman tests + logistic AUC.
[2026-09-20 10:42:01 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 011]   D4  Resonant substructure: for a trial perturber axis a9 in
[2026-09-20 10:42:01 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 011]   300-900 AU, does the observed a-set sit preferentially at
[2026-09-20 10:42:01 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 011]   mean-motion resonances (period ratios near small-integer p/q)?
[2026-09-20 10:42:01 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 011]   Statistic: mean distance of (a/a9)^{3/2} to the nearest small
[2026-09-20 10:42:01 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 011]   rational, calibrated by Monte-Carlo.
[2026-09-20 10:42:01 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 011]   D5  Sharp-edge test: does the transition between aligned and
[2026-09-20 10:42:01 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 011]   unaligned objects occur sharply at a boundary in perihelion
[2026-09-20 10:42:01 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 011]   direction space (wall), or smoothly (shepherd)?
[2026-09-20 10:42:01 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 011]   D6  Cross-population: Centaurs (class CEN) -- the Neptune-coupled
[2026-09-20 10:42:01 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 011]   population -- should show no axis; outer comets are checked for a
[2026-09-20 10:42:01 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 011]   preferred perihelion axis for comparison with the TNO axis.
